From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] serialize DBR component lifetime with PDEV destruction

Static audit after 0031 found that DBR response events, CFR/Spectral module
unregister, and the object-manager PDEV destroy callback can share the same
ring and buffer pointers without a common lifetime gate. Add a PDEV-locked
component lookup, explicit active-user count, destroy gate, and per-module
unregister gate. PDEV destruction waits for in-flight callbacks before ring
deinit and never frees the component after a bounded wait timeout. This
changes host lifetime ordering only; no firmware command values or packet
formats. Requires static/build validation before RAM testing.

